<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: the target of a jump thunk is a function entry
    (`option thunkentry on|off`, default-ON).

    Issue:      kuna GH-992 - functions behind `jmp rel32` thunks are never
                function starts (MSVC /INCREMENTAL).  The Listing walk makes a
                function only at a CALL target, so a routine reached only
                through a `jmp` thunk was attributed to the thunk.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the Listing walk's committed function
                set (`listing/kuna_thunkentry.rs`, folded into `fast_funcdisc`
                and `funcdisc_recursive`).
    P0 assert:  `option thunkentry on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  Every pass clears
    it and loads `thunk_table_pe_i386.exe` (source `thunk_table_pe_i386.asm`
    beside it): three 5-byte `jmp rel32` thunks at 0x401000 / 0x401005 /
    0x40100a, then sum at 0x401010 (push ebp frame), leaf at 0x401030 (no
    frame) and start at 0x401040.  The entry point and every call go to a
    thunk; nothing calls a body directly.

    Pass 1 (`mode fast`, `option thunkentry off`) reproduces the bug: the
    inventory is the three thunks and no body.
    Pass 2 (`mode fast`, shipped default) lists sum, leaf and start, and leaf
    decompiles to its own body.
    Pass 3 (`mode aggressive`, `option thunkentry off`) finds sum and start
    only through the prologue scan; leaf, which has no prologue, is missing.
    Pass 4 (`mode aggressive`, shipped default) finds leaf too.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/thunk_table_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>mode fast</com>
  <com>option thunkentry off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/thunk_table_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>mode fast</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>load function sub_401030</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/thunk_table_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>mode aggressive</com>
  <com>option thunkentry off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/thunk_table_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>mode aggressive</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>phase catalog thunkentry</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUNKENTRY #1: every thunk is a function in all four passes" min="12" max="12">0x40100[05a] sub_40100[05a]</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUNKENTRY #2: sum and start are missing only from pass 1 (fast, option off)" min="6" max="6">0x4010[14]0 sub_4010[14]0</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUNKENTRY #3: leaf is a function only with the option on, in fast and aggressive mode" min="2" max="2">0x401030 sub_401030</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUNKENTRY #4: leaf decompiles to its own body" min="1" max="1">return a0 \+ 7;</stringmatch>
